If you're doing "zoom" to up the size of the tiles,
then just using a larger tile set and including its
name and size into the appropriate OPTION
declarations in the nethackrc.gnome file should do
the trick. If you're in need of bigger text for
menus too, I don't know how to do that.

Since I played using KDE instead of Gnome, and that
long ago (I'm stuck with WinXP right now -- bletch),
I really don't know how to do the tile set change
either, I remember it being fairly hard to figure
out where to put the new tiles so the game could
find them and would respect your tile choice. There
are a wide variety of tile sets available online,
the Absurd Tile set has them in sizes up to 128x128
pixels for a single tile, for example. If you can't
find a size you like send me email and I can mail
you one of those for your experiments to see if you
can make it work.

